AB  - As the Architecture, Engineering, and Construction (AEC) industry increasingly adopts robotic technologies, the need for intuitive and efficient Human-Robot Interaction (HRI) becomes crucial. This paper introduces a multimodal interaction system, utilizing Virtual Reality (VR) to facilitate collaboration. The system effectively integrates speech and VR controller inputs, allowing construction workers to provide simple commands for interaction with robots. The system transcends the limitations of speech-only interfaces by enabling users to point at objects with VR controllers while issuing commands through natural language. This study also integrates ChatGPT, one of the large language models, enabling bi-directional communication for HRI. By optimizing ChatGPT prompts for construction tasks and using multimodal inputs, users are able to enhance the accuracy of instructions and ensure that the execution of tasks is in alignment with their intended outcomes. This study includes a demonstration of the proposed interaction system through an application in drywall installation. The findings highlight the effectiveness of such multimodal VR Interfaces with advanced AI technologies to support HRC in the construction sector. © ASCE.
