AB  - Advanced extended reality (XR) technologies in psychomotor skill learning (PSL) offer promising implications to accelerate the learning process and enhance learning outcomes. The proposed prototype explores the intricate PSL mechanisms focusing on mental processing and motor body movements to achieve deeper PSL. The design of XR technology aligns with generative learning theory driving both mental processing and motor processing in PSL, with a goal to foster more effective and efficient PSL. © ISLS.
