AB  - With the advancement of robust network connections and the rise of live streaming platforms, it has become possible to experience local events and walking tours remotely in real-time. This study introduces a city-wide audio augmented reality system designed to enhance engagement at local festivals by combining livestreamed video with character-driven commentaries on local history and event details. To ensure continuous storytelling, even in areas with few points of interest, this study proposes a novel geofencing architecture that considers multilayered city features, enabling seamless audio guide experiences. Additionally, this paper introduces prompt engineering for generating entertaining and listener-friendly guide scripts, tailored for large language models, named the geofence-to-conversation technique. A preliminary study of our prototype system, deployed at an actual local festival, demonstrates its effectiveness and potential for enhancing regional promotion. © 2024 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
