AB  - The integration of local linear mapping (LLM) into art resource processing offers efficient extraction and classification of intricate art laboratory features, laying a data foundation for future resource sharing and cross-border integration. This article strives to enhance the precision and user satisfaction of art image feature recognition by presenting a 3D visualization algorithm that combines LLM with virtual reality (VR). Our ultimate goal is to foster the expansion of art education and resource sharing. Initially, we establish a 3D visualization model that leverages LLM and VR, enabling the extraction and showcase of nonlinear art image features for a more immersive and lifelike visual experience. Exhaustive experimental outcomes confirm that our algorithm and platform offer superior accuracy, richer artistic resources, and an elevated user experience in the realm of art education and resource sharing. © 2024 IEEE.
