AB  - With the continuous development of the field of industrial design, intelligent technology plays an increasingly important role in improving design efficiency and innovation. First, through an in-depth needs analysis, the challenges and issues facing the field of industrial design are identified. Subsequently, a large amount of diversity data related to industrial design was collected and prepared to provide a strong support for system training. In terms of model selection, through comprehensive consideration of different architectures of GAN, models suitable for specific tasks are selected and carefully trained. For a user-friendly interactive experience, an intuitive user interface has been designed to make it easy for designers to upload design requirements, view generated results and provide feedback. The system integrates advanced technology such as computer aided design and virtual reality, which improves the comprehensiveness and practicability of the system. In order to promote the continuous improvement of system performance, feedback mechanism and continuous experimental optimization process are introduced. At the same time, security and privacy concerns are taken into account to ensure that the designed and generated data is properly handled. Finally, the effectiveness of the system is verified, and documentation and training materials are provided to support designers to make full use of the system. In summary, this study provides a complete and feasible method for the development of intelligent industrial design assistance system, and makes a positive contribution to the innovation and improvement of design efficiency in the field of industrial design. © 2024 IEEE.
