AB  - This paper presents the development of a humanized, adaptive, emotionally expressive 3D avatar capable of real-time conversational interaction. The avatar system integrates a transformer-based language model (FLAN-T5) for natural language understanding, an emotion classification model (Go Emotions) for detecting user affect, a medical-domain model (BioBERT) for healthcare support, and a pitch-modulated text-to-speech engine (Coqui TTS) for expressive voice output. The avatar, designed with Character Creator 4 and animated in Unity, uses blendshape facial expressions to reflect emotional states such as happiness, sadness, surprise, and neutrality. A custom Unity interface manages user input and displays chat history while synchronizing audio and animation. The backend, built with Python and Flask, bridges AI processing and real-time rendering. Survey results show that emotion-aware responses significantly enhance user perception of empathy, intelligence, and engagement. The system demonstrates a scalable foundation for emotionally intelligent virtual agents in healthcare assistive applications. © 2025 IEEE.
