AB  - This paper introduces a lightweight AI-assisted framework that converts disassembly videos into interactive augmented reality (AR) repair guidance, supporting novice users who often struggle with part organization and reassembly sequencing during household repairs. Our system integrates vision-language models in a multi-agent pipeline to automatically extract procedural steps, component identities, and spatial relationships from user-recorded videos during disassembly, enabling it to support diverse products while reducing AR authoring effort. In an initial evaluation with six products, the system correctly identified 29 of 32 components and produced accurate task descriptions, showing its potential for cross-product repair support. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
