AB  - An increasing prevalence of dual-income households has posed challenges to maintaining consistent educational engagement and companionship in early childhood. To address this issue, we introduced the intelligent parenting assistance and books and nurturing (iPABan) robot that has an interactive companion system designed to support the cognitive and emotional development of children aged 2 to 10 years. iPABan enhances early childhood education by generating personalized stories, images, and voiceovers in a parental tone, utilizing a language model with a capability similar to to Phi-3. This functionality enables the creation of audiovisual narratives that emulate the warmth and expressiveness of parents, thereby fostering a more immersive and emotionally resonant learning experience. iPABan integrates virtual touch and gesture recognition powered by edge AI, facilitating real-time interaction in mixed reality. The fusion of physical and digital modalities allows children to engage actively with educational content, promoting enriched learning through play. By seamlessly bridging the real and virtual worlds, iPABan offers a multifaceted platform that delivers companionship, entertainment, and pedagogical support in an intuitive and interactive format. © 2025 IEEE.
