AB  - Traditional e-book reading lacks the shared sensory experiences that deepen engagement. We present a system that transforms virtual reading into a dynamic, multisensory, collaborative experience. Our system integrates Virtual Reality (VR), haptics, generative audio, and physiological sensing to create a shared environment that reacts to the e-book’s narrative and the readers’ emotional state. As users read and discuss a story, the system analyses their conversation sentiment and physiological arousal to dynamically generate VR visuals, soundscape, and haptic events, providing shared embodied anchors for key narrative moments. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
