UR  - https://doi.org/10.1145/3770445.3770477
AB  - Objective: Based on the unique interactive characteristics of augmented reality (AR) technology, this study explores its application in the design research of cultural heritage protection and inheritance. By leveraging AR's advantages, such as efficient user experience, integration of the real and virtual worlds, and overlaying of virtual and real information, this study aims to investigate new approaches to cultural heritage protection and inheritance. Method: This study analyzes existing AR application cases both domestically and internationally, explores the role of AR technology in the field of cultural heritage protection and inheritance, and summarizes the design principles of AR technology in cultural heritage protection and inheritance projects. Taking Suzhou's cultural heritage as an example, this study conducts AR project design and implementation targeting cultural heritage, and through the project, conducts empirical research to prove the practical feasibility of the design principles, providing some reference for the application of AR technology in cultural heritage protection and inheritance. Results: AR technology has to some extent addressed the challenges posed by traditional preservation methods, effectively enhancing the public's understanding of cultural heritage and their willingness to participate, and promoting the revitalization and diversified utilization of cultural heritage. Conclusion: This study validated the advantages of AR technology in the preservation and inheritance of cultural heritage, confirming that AR technology can promote the preservation and inheritance of cultural heritage and endow it with new vitality.
