AB  - Ensemble musical performances demand both technical precision - such as exact fingerings, intonation, and tempo - as well as higher-order skills such as active listening, real-time responsiveness, and emotional expression. This study explored the ways that generative AI and VR could be used to facilitate this complex interplay of cognitive and expressive demands. We conducted a needs-finding pilot study with four advanced viola students who rehearsed in a gallery-style virtual concert hall accompanied by a smartphone-based AI partner. Post-rehearsal interviews underwent thematic analysis to identify key system requirements for simulating an effective ensemble partner. Three core needs emerged: (1) faithful interpretation of score arrangements to support expressive nuance, (2) adaptive sensory feedback to enhance VR immersion, and (3) pre-rehearsal exchange of emotional intent. The insights gained in this study could guide the development of AI/VR systems aimed at augmenting ensemble practice, supporting iterative rehearsal in immersive environments that complement human musicianship. © 2025 ACM.
