AB  - This hands-on workshop invites participants to co-design conceptual "recipes"for immersive experiences across four creative sectors: urban environments, museums and heritage, journalism and entertainment, and physical games and play. Drawing on the metaphor of a cookbook, participants will engage with XR "ingredients"(technologies, content types, interaction modes) and "cooking techniques"(design strategies, generative AI, spatial augmentation) to develop speculative but grounded prototypes. The workshop combines creative worldbuilding, AI-assisted co-creation, and participatory design methods to reflect on XR's spatial, inclusive, and experiential dimensions. Framed within the traditions of participatory design, speculative design, spatial theory, and experience-centered research, the session explores XR as a socially situated, layered medium. Outcomes will contribute to an evolving Immersive XR Cookbook and support broader research on low-threshold, context-sensitive XR design. This workshop is developed as part of the research activities of the NEXR (Next Extended Reality) project, which explores accessible, culturally grounded, and sector-specific XR adoption in Finland's creative industries. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
