AB  - In the digital age, the living transmission of intangible cultural heritage faces an urgent need for transformation. Generative artificial intelligence offers efficient visual generation solutions for traditional clothing design; however, current applications largely remain limited to superficial generation, lacking precise translation of complex cultural elements and quantitative evaluation of user perception. This paper proposes a closed-loop framework for AIGC-driven ICH interactive design based on the Kano model. Using Cantonese embroidery and new Chinese-style luggage as case studies, the framework establishes a semantic mapping mechanism that translates the implicit craftsmanship of Cantonese embroidery into prompts for large language models, thereby generating high-fidelity visual prototypes. and conducting quantitative measurements of audience perception preferences via Kano Model questionnaires. The aim is to break through the barriers of traditional generative design's heavy reliance on subjective experience, providing scientific design methods and strategic insights for the cross-disciplinary integration and commercial transformation of intangible cultural heritage in the digital age.
