TI  - AR-EpiAid: An Augmented Reality Decision Support System for Real-Time Interpretation of Multimodal Epilepsy Data
PY  - 2026
T2  - 2026 International Conference on Artificial Intelligence, Computer, Data Sciences and Applications (ACDSA)
SP  - 1
EP  - 8
DO  - 10.1109/ACDSA67686.2026.11468245
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105037618063?origin=resultslist
AB  - The diagnosis of epilepsy necessitates a combination of diverse clinical data, encompassing electroencephalography (EEG), structural and functional neuroimaging, and unstructured clinical record. Present procedures depend on disjointed 2D displays that impose a significant cognitive load on doctors, who are required to mentally integrate multimodal information under time constraints. This conceptual paper introduces AR-EpiAid, an augmented reality (AR) framework aimed at integrating EEGderived cortical activity maps, MRI reconstructions, and clinical summaries generated by large language models (LLMs) into a cohesive spatial environment. The study delineates the proposed architecture of the system, prospective clinical uses, anticipated benefits, and significant obstacles associated with data processing, hardware limitations, interoperability, and regulatory constraints, however no implementation is presented. AR-EpiAid intends to function as a framework for forthcoming research investigating how AR technologies may improve interpretability, alleviate cognitive load, and facilitate decision-making in epilepsy care. © 2026 IEEE.
