AB  - Novice ceramic makers often struggle to bridge early-stage inspiration with feasible physical making, particularly when transitioning from ideation to embodied shaping and surface decoration. To address this challenge, we present ARtisanAI, an integrated AI and AR workflow that supports the full ceramic design-to-craft process across three stages: ideation, shaping, and decoration. We implement ARtisanAI as a functional prototype that enables users to generate inspectable 3D references from hand-drawn sketches and receive in-situ AR scaffolding throughout the making process. In a mixed-methods user study (N=16), questionnaire responses and semi-structured interviews reveal stage-dependent complementarity between the two technologies: AI proved most beneficial for expanding the design space during ideation, while AR was most effective for supporting shaping consistency in situ. Participants further identified opportunities to enhance color planning and glazing guidance in future iterations. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
