AB  - This article highlights the possibilities that artificial intelligence (AI) holds for creating innovative animated Shakespeare adaptations. It focuses on three examples: an adaptation of Pericles, Prince of Tyre for virtual reality that employs AI to enhance player interaction; ShakesVR, which uses AI for guided navigation through a hybrid narrative of three plays; and the use of AI to animate nineteenth-century Shakespeare illustrations, addressing concerns regarding generative AI and artistic integrity. The discussion proposes that responsible integration of AI into animation results in collaborative creativity that can enhance storytelling and creative production while respecting ethical considerations. © The Author(s) 2026
