AB  - This paper outlines preliminary lessons from integrating a voice user interface Teaching Assistant into an educational virtual reality game with Large Language Model support. The Teaching Assistant appropriately handled unclear or garbled utterances and could correctly interpret compound "macro"commands, even if the subcommands were provided out of sequence, referred to past actions, or were multilingual.In a user study of 20 participants, players rated the game as easy to use, easy to learn, and highly engaging. Notably, the Teaching Assistant error-corrected 78% of misheard utterances. However, players tended to overestimate its abilities, which sometimes led to hallucinations and misinformation. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
