AB  - Location-based immersive theatre faces scalability challenges. VR offers a solution, yet current systems fail to simultaneously achieve low-latency multimodal responsiveness, narrative coherence under user agency, and character consistency across extended improvisation with Embodied Conversational Agents (ECAs). We present a VR-AI Director framework deployed in EveryMacbeth, a VR re-staging of Shakespeare's Macbeth. The framework integrates (1) parallel scheduling reducing response latency by 81.6%, (2) a Trust Value-driven Procedural Narrative Mechanism, and (3) a Machinery Narrative Audit protocol that reduced persona drift from 8/15 to 2/15 significant shifts through iterative prompt refine-ment - enabling scalable, coherent VR immersive theatre. © 2026 IEEE.
