AB  - This entry explores the English for Specific Purposes (ESP) approach to language teaching, focusing on its four key pillars: needs analysis, learning objectives, materials and methods, and evaluation. The entry bridges linguistic theory with practical applications in both academia and industry. It also considers the dynamic and continually evolving nature of the field, as well as the impact of new tools, technologies, and interdisciplinary approaches, including corpus methods, data-driven learning (DDL), generative AI (GenAI), and virtual reality. © 2026 Elsevier Ltd. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies.
