AB  - We present a mixed reality system that complements cultural heritage narrations with on-the-fly 3D visualizations. Our implementation for the HoloLens head-mounted display automatically extracts information about narrated objects and applies Shap-E to generate corresponding visualizations, which are rendered within the user's field of view as the narration progresses. Unlike other systems that require explicit user input, our system operates passively for laid-back consumption of visually enhanced narrations. In an evaluation involving a 23-minute cultural heritage podcast, our system generated a total of 88 visual augmentations, approximately one at every 15 seconds. Based on our results, we outline future work opportunities in automatic augmentation of audio narrations with visual representations toward novel mixed reality experiences for cultural heritage. © 2026 IEEE.
