AB  - In this paper, we present a virtual reality (VR) system for ophthalmic science popularization, built with the Unity 3D engine and deployed on the PICO 4 VR headset. The system integrates four interactive modules: a knowledge quiz zone, an anatomical visualization lab, an eye relaxation zone, and a video education theater. Each module is designed to deliver an interactive, experiential, and practical learning experience. We describe the key technical solutions, including spaced repetition quizzes, focus-shifting training, interactive exploration of eye models, and immersive video learning. In addition, large language models are employed to generate popular science content, with manual review to ensure reliability and accuracy. Our work demonstrates the potential of VR as a powerful tool for public ophthalmic science popularization and offers a reusable framework for future VR-based health education research. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
