AB  - This chapter examines the intersection of generative artificial intelligence and immersive virtual reality as a transformative shift in the communicative structure of architectural representation. It aims to reconceptualize representation not as a linear process ofvisual production but as a multilayeredsystem ofmediation through which spatial meaning is progressively constructed. The chapter outlines how linguistic input, algorithmic interpretation, visual synthesis, volumetric modeling, and immersive experience operate as interconnected stages within a unified framework. Through this perspective, representation is positioned as a dynamic and iterative process shaped by feedback loops between human intention and computational systems. The proposed AI–IVR mediated framework highlights how design knowledge is generated, evaluated, and reformulated across semantic, visual, geometric, and experiential domains, offering a conceptual model for understanding contemporary interior architectural practice. Copyright © 2027, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. Copying or distributing in print or electronic forms without written permission of IGI Global Scientific Publishing is prohibited. Use of this chapter to train generative artificial intelligence (AI) technologies is expressly prohibited. The publisher reserves all rights to license its use for generative AI training and machine learning model development.
