AB  - The growing use of head-mounted AR devices has produced a surge of egocentric recordings of procedural tasks - step-by-step activities such as medical procedures - creating rich opportunities for performance analysis. Yet current analyses are time-consuming, requiring substantial manual inspection to identify events, actions, and objects from videos, with little automated support for surfacing insights or errors. We introduce InsightAR, a visual analytics tool that integrates event detection, action recognition, and multi-modal language models to create video summaries capturing key errors and insights. Its interface further enables users to refine generated insights and errors collaboratively. A user study (N=16) found that InsightAR identifies significantly more errors and marginally significant insight numbers than the baseline. Our work demonstrated the feasibility and potential benefits of future human-AI collaborative video analysis. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
