SP  - 511
EP  - 515
PB  - Association for Computing Machinery
DO  - 10.1145/3777730.3777812
UR  - https://doi.org/10.1145/3777730.3777812
AB  - This paper addresses the challenges of insufficient style consistency and low detail fidelity in artistic style image generation. We propose an intelligent art creation method based on a deep convolutional generative adversarial network (DCGAN). Building on the traditional GAN framework, our method incorporates multi-layer convolutional feature fusion and style optimization modules to enhance the generated images' ability to capture the target artist's style. We construct a comprehensive technical system consisting of data preprocessing, feature extraction, generative model training, and style optimization, and conduct experimental validation on image data from a variety of artists' works. Experimental results demonstrate that the proposed method outperforms existing mainstream approaches on Inception Score (IS), Frechet Inception Distance (FID), and Structural Similarity (SSIM). FID is reduced by 12.7% and SSIM is improved by 8.4%, demonstrating significant advantages in detail representation and style restoration. This research not only improves the applicability of generative models in artistic creation but also provides a new technical path for intelligent and personalized art generation.
