AB  - Conventional generative painting methods lack interactivity and instructional support. Those based on image style transfer or static synthesis are largely result-focused, with insufficient process visualization and real-time feedback - impeding step-by-step technique training. Restricted to 2D interfaces, they also have weak immersion and low engagement, limiting their painting-teaching potential. To address this, we propose an interactive art experience system integrating a stroke-by-stroke AI painting model and AR. Via frame-by-frame stroke trajectory rendering and a Unity3D-based real-time virtual interface, it enables immersive painting participation. Its stroke prompt and detection module evaluates color selection and stroke positioning in real time, guiding users through a progressive "observation-imitation-feedback"learning path. User studies validated its painting-teaching potential (especially in instructional design, interaction experience, and immersive learning): 84% perceived it as innovative and engaging; painting guidance scored 4.1/5, interactive convenience 4.0/5, and 64% recognized AR-enhanced immersion, alongside other positive feedback. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
