AB  - This work creates and implements an AI-powered psychological therapy system for adolescents, focused on a virtual persona dubbed “Teacher Xiaohua.” Through guided talks, the system assists teenagers in expressing their inner thoughts, identifying issues linked to learning, emotions, stress, and family communication, and creating mental health assessment reports to provide scientific counsel and therapies for psychological well-being. The system combines advanced AI technologies and finely crafted interface methods. A guided conversational framework and a multi-level subject change system provide natural and fluid talks. The employment of an anime-style virtual character increases engagement and accessibility. The system uses large language models (LLMs) to create responses, includes historical data for contextual memory, and provides an emotionally engaged experience via the virtual character. The virtual character's expressions and movements are managed by the VTube Studio platform, which is often used in VTuber scenarios. Pre-designed expression templates, audio-driven synchronization, and the random insertion of dynamic effects enable realistic interactions. Furthermore, the system conducts detailed evaluations of users’ mental states by extracting keywords and quantifying evaluation criteria, resulting in individualized recommendations. Testing shows that the system has tremendous potential in mental health assessment, providing a friendly and efficient mental health support tool for adolescents while also paving a new research path for technological innovation in the field of psychological counseling.
