AB  - Generative Artificial Intelligence (AI) has opened up new possibilities for efficiency innovation in film and television visual effects (VFX) production. The traditional VFX production process involves creative design via hand-drawing or Photoshop in the early stage, followed by 3D modeling based on the design drafts, and finally rendering. This process is often time-consuming and inefficient. This paper proposes a VFX production method that integrates AI with the traditional workflow, namely “Doubao AI for rendering generation → Tripo AI for preliminary modeling → Maya for model refinement and animation production → Unreal Engine for rendering”. The feasibility and advantages of this model are verified through comparative experiments. The experimental results show that the most prominent role of AI in film and television VFX production lies in early-stage creative divergence and auxiliary modeling. It can effectively improve production efficiency while ensuring work quality, providing an efficient production mode for the film and television post-production workflow.
