AB  - Aiming at the characteristics of fragmented user needs and diversified cultural expression forms of cultural digital products, this paper proposes an intelligent adaptive UI model integrating Generative Artificial Intelligence (Generative AI) and multimodal perception technology. [1]The model constructs a multimodal cultural demand feature extraction network to realize cross-modal fusion computation of text, image and behavior data.[2] It also builds a dynamic generation and optimization mechanism for UI elements based on Generative Adversarial Networks (GAN) and Reinforcement Learning (RL). [3]Experiments show that the model outperforms traditional methods in cultural demand recognition accuracy (F1-score reaching 0.89), UI adaptation response speed (average reduction of 37%) and user satisfaction (increase of 28%). [4]It provides technical support from computer science and engineering for intelligent interaction design of cultural digital products.[8]
