AB  - We introduce StoryBaker, a generative system for constructing memoryscapes, spatialized representations of personal narratives. StoryBaker enables everyday, non-technical users to externalize lived experiences as XR memoryscapes by translating narrative and emotional elements into spatial layouts, objects, sound, and interaction. Leveraging multimodal generative models and affective design frameworks, the system maps emotional and narrative cues onto spatial structures that support reflection and exploration. Through a preliminary pilot study, we probe how users engage with the generated memoryscapes of their own and others', highlighting opportunities and challenges in emotional fidelity, symbolic interaction, and perspective-taking. We discuss the implications of using XR as a medium for memory representation and outline future directions for generative approaches to spatial memory in immersive systems. © 2026 IEEE.
